\":\"Explore more models\",\"data-_gt\":\"$undefined\"}]\n7c:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+129px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] lg:scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+70px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] mb-10 last:mb-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-1.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-book-open h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"path\",\"1akyts\",{\"d\":\"M12 7v14\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"ruj8y\",{\"d\":\"M3 18a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5a4 4 0 0 1 4 4 4 4 0 0 1 4-4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-6a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-3-3z\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-medium\",\"children\":\"Documentation\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],null]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-4 max-w-2xl text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground\",\"children\":\"Guides, cookbooks, and tools for building with OpenAI: GPT-6 Luna on OpenRouter.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border border-none p-0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L85\",null,{\"resources\":[{\"type\":\"cookbook\",\"title\":\"GPT-6 Migration Guide\",\"href\":\"/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/model-migrations/gpt-6\"}],\"page\":\"model\"}]}]]}]\n7d:[[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"id\":\"faq\",\"className\":\"scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+129px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] lg:scroll-mt-[calc(var(--navbar-height)+70px+var(--sticky-banner-top,0px))] mb-10 last:mb-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"ref\":\"$undefined\",\"xmlns\":\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",\"width\":24,\"height\":24,\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"className\":\"lucide lucide-circle-question-mark h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-muted-foreground\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"circle\",\"1mglay\",{\"cx\":\"12\",\"cy\":\"12\",\"r\":\"10\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"1u773s\",{\"d\":\"M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3\"}],[\"$\",\"path\",\"p32p05\",{\"d\":\"M12 17h.01\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-base font-medium\",\"children\":\"Frequently asked questions\"}],\"$undefined\"]}],null]}],null,[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"rounded-lg border border-border border-none p-0\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L86\",null,{\"faqs\":[{\"question\":\"What is GPT-6 Luna?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna is the fast, cost-efficient model in OpenAI's GPT-6 series, positioned below GPT-6 Sol. It is suited for high-volume and latency-sensitive workloads such as chat, classification, and lightweight agentic tasks, and at higher reasoning effort it can take on complex software engineering and computer-use tasks that previously called for a Sol-tier model.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"Where is the GPT-6 Luna documentation?\",\"answer\":\"The GPT-6 Luna documentation on OpenRouter includes the [GPT-6 Migration Guide](/docs/cookbook/evaluate-and-optimize/model-migrations/gpt-6) cookbook. The [quickstart](/docs/quickstart) covers API keys and your first request, and the [API reference](/docs/api-reference/overview) lists every parameter.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"How much does GPT-6 Luna cost?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna costs $0.10/M input tokens and $0.50/M output tokens, with separate rates for Cache Read at $0.01/M tokens, Cache Write at $0.125/M tokens, and Web Search at $10.00/1K calls.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"What is the context length of GPT-6 Luna?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna has a 1,050,000 token context window. It supports up to 128,000 completion tokens.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"Does GPT-6 Luna support tool calling and structured outputs?\",\"answer\":\"Yes. GPT-6 Luna accepts `tools` and `tool_choice` for function calling. It also supports structured outputs via a JSON schema in `response_format`.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"Can I disable prompt caching for GPT-6 Luna?\",\"answer\":\"Yes. OpenAI caches prompts of 1024 tokens or more automatically, and GPT-6 Luna bills a cache write on each cached prompt whether or not the cached prefix is read again. To turn caching off for a request, set `prompt_cache_options.mode` to `\\\"explicit\\\"` at the request root and do not mark any content block with `prompt_cache_breakpoint`. Explicit mode disables OpenAI-managed breakpoints, so a request with none of your own has no cacheable prefix and is billed at the plain input rate. See the [prompt caching guide](/docs/guides/best-practices/prompt-caching#disabling-prompt-caching).\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"What inputs and outputs does GPT-6 Luna support?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna accepts files such as PDFs, images, and text as input and returns text.\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"Which providers serve GPT-6 Luna?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna is served by 3 providers on OpenRouter: OpenAI, Azure, and Amazon Bedrock. Requests are routed to the best available provider, with automatic failover to the others, and you can pin or exclude providers with [provider routing](/docs/features/provider-routing).\",\"isCustom\":false},{\"question\":\"When was GPT-6 Luna released?\",\"answer\":\"GPT-6 Luna was released on September 22, 2026.\",\"isCustom\":false}],\"modelPermaslug\":\"openai/gpt-6-luna-20260922\",\"modelSlug\":\"openai/gpt-6-luna\"}]}]]}],\"$L87\"]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"88:Tb83,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is GPT-6 Luna?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna is the fast, cost-efficient model in OpenAI's GPT-6 series, positioned below GPT-6 Sol. It is suited for high-volume and latency-sensitive workloads such as chat, classification, and lightweight agentic tasks, and at higher reasoning effort it can take on complex software engineering and computer-use tasks that previously called for a Sol-tier model.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Where is the GPT-6 Luna documentation?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The GPT-6 Luna documentation on OpenRouter includes the GPT-6 Migration Guide cookbook. The quickstart covers API keys and your first request, and the API reference lists every parameter.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How much does GPT-6 Luna cost?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna costs $0.10/M input tokens and $0.50/M output tokens, with separate rates for Cache Read at $0.01/M tokens, Cache Write at $0.125/M tokens, and Web Search at $10.00/1K calls.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the context length of GPT-6 Luna?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna has a 1,050,000 token context window. It supports up to 128,000 completion tokens.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does GPT-6 Luna support tool calling and structured outputs?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. GPT-6 Luna accepts tools and tool_choice for function calling. It also supports structured outputs via a JSON schema in response_format.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I disable prompt caching for GPT-6 Luna?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. OpenAI caches prompts of 1024 tokens or more automatically, and GPT-6 Luna bills a cache write on each cached prompt whether or not the cached prefix is read again. To turn caching off for a request, set prompt_cache_options.mode to \\\"explicit\\\" at the request root and do not mark any content block with prompt_cache_breakpoint. Explicit mode disables OpenAI-managed breakpoints, so a request with none of your own has no cacheable prefix and is billed at the plain input rate. See the prompt caching guide.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What inputs and outputs does GPT-6 Luna support?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna accepts files such as PDFs, images, and text as input and returns text.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which providers serve GPT-6 Luna?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna is served by 3 providers on OpenRouter: OpenAI, Azure, and Amazon Bedrock. Requests are routed to the best available provider, with automatic failover to the others, and you can pin or exclude providers with provider routing.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"When was GPT-6 Luna released?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"GPT-6 Luna was released on September 22, 2026.\"}}]}87:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$88\"}}]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"89:I[743425,[\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1zet098htcd4i.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ncwfr4wdrrub.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/2xgvr_umi0kh_.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/0fm-u2k-im7-i.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1m2s60egjx067.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1xgt1odsntw54.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/2osv2vgv9ppxf.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3d265-i4j720s.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3d304w99n_8rh.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/1ean_2r1sqb1a.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable/chunks/3x8ioig9pq1hs.js\",\"/_next/static/immutable